    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "THE RADIO",
      "narration_text": "Then the radio. Classic Bluetooth hops between seventy-nine channels, up to sixteen hundred times a second, and shares them with Wi-Fi. In my simulation, a busy Wi-Fi network made seventeen percent of tries fail. Adaptive hopping skips the busy channels: about one percent.",
