    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "CODECS",
      "narration_text": "Your phone and headphones agree on a codec. SBC is the baseline. Apple's devices prefer AAC. Many Android phones also offer aptX, at about three hundred and fifty kilobits, or LDAC, at up to nine hundred and ninety. More data can sound better, but it's harder to send without gaps.",
