    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "THE BUFFER",
      "narration_text": "Lost packets, from Wi-Fi or your own body, get sent again, so the earbuds keep a little music in reserve: a buffer. In two minutes of my simulation, a fifty millisecond buffer glitched thirty times; two hundred, three times; three hundred, never. That reserve is the main reason Bluetooth lags. Listen: small, then big.",
